/-!
# The Segre product of projective spectra and fibre products of projective schemes

Let `A = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} 𝒜 d` and `B = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} ℬ d` be `ℕ`-graded `R`-algebras. Their Segre product
`Segre 𝒜 ℬ = ⨁_{d ≥ 0} (𝒜 d ⊗[R] ℬ d)` (`TauCeti.GradedAlgebra.Segre`) has standard affine charts
`D₊(a ⊗ₜ b)` (`a ∈ 𝒜 d`, `b ∈ ℬ d`, `d > 0`) whose coordinate rings are canonically isomorphic to
`A_{(a)} ⊗[R] B_{(b)}` (`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.segreEquiv`). Gluing the chart projections
produces canonical morphisms `Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ) ⟶ Proj 𝒜` and
`Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ) ⟶ Proj ℬ` over `Spec R` exhibiting `Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ)` as the
scheme-theoretic fibre product `Proj 𝒜 ×_{Spec R} Proj ℬ`. No finite-generation, degree-one
generation, or flatness hypothesis on `A` or `B` is needed for this cartesian square.

Combining the Segre cartesian square with degree-one generation of `Segre 𝒜 ℬ`
(`TauCeti.GradedAlgebra.Segre.grading_subset_adjoin_range_linearMap`) and closed immersions into
symmetric-algebra projective spaces (`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isClosedImmersion_map_gradedLift`)
gives the permanence properties of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsProjectiveOver R`:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsProjectiveOver.of_proj`: `Proj 𝒜` is projective over `R` whenever a
  linear map from a finite `R`-module into `𝒜 1` generates `𝒜` in positive degrees over `R`;
* `(Proj I.quotientGrading).IsProjectiveOver R`: the projective spectrum of a homogeneous quotient
  of `R[X₀, …, Xₙ]` is projective over `R`;
* `(Spec (.of R)).IsProjectiveOver R`: the affine base `Spec R` is projective over `R`;
* `(pullback (X ↘ Spec (.of R)) (Y ↘ Spec (.of R))).IsProjectiveOver R`: the fibre product over
  `Spec R` of two projective schemes over `R` is projective over `R`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.segreAffineOpenCover`: the affine open cover of
  `Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ)` by the pure-tensor charts `D₊(a ⊗ₜ b)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.segreFst`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.segreSnd`: the canonical projections
  from `Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ)` to `Proj 𝒜` and `Proj ℬ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.segreIso`: the canonical isomorphism
  `Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ) ≅ pullback (toSpecCoeff 𝒜) (toSpecCoeff ℬ)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isPullback_segre`: `Proj (Segre.grading 𝒜 ℬ)` is the fibre product of
  `Proj 𝒜` and `Proj ℬ` over `Spec R`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IsProjectiveOver.of_proj`: projectivity criterion for `Proj 𝒜` from
  finite degree-one generation in positive degrees.
* the instances `(Proj I.quotientGrading).IsProjectiveOver R`, `(Spec (.of R)).IsProjectiveOver R`,
  and `(pullback (X ↘ Spec (.of R)) (Y ↘ Spec (.of R))).IsProjectiveOver R`.

## References

* A. Grothendieck, *Éléments de géométrie algébrique. II. Étude globale élémentaire de quelques
  classes de morphismes*, Publ. Math. IHÉS 8 (1961), §3.1.4 and Proposition 3.1.8.
* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Exercise II.5.11 and Section II.4.
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 27.11.3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0), closed immersions of
  projective spectra from degree-one generation.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits HomogeneousLocalization
